WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:02.969
-The president held his first
rally in months on Saturday

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:05.338
in an attempt to project
political strength

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:08.742
as his administration faces
a series of crises.

00:00:08.742 --> 00:00:10.276
Instead, it was a flop,
and I should say

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:11.978
I get that he wanted to go out
and see people.

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:14.013
I've been in an attic
for three months.

00:00:14.013 --> 00:00:15.882
I miss having guests.

00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:18.784
Zoom is great.
It's not face to face.

00:00:18.784 --> 00:00:21.187
But I deal with it because there
isn't a better option.

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:23.188
It's not like there's a magic
door behind me

00:00:23.188 --> 00:00:25.658
that'll send me a guest if I say
their name three times.

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:28.461
Ethan Hawke! Ethan Hawke!
Ethan Hawke!

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:30.029
Right?
I mean, that would be stupid,

00:00:30.029 --> 00:00:32.564
but also, I mean,
I mean, how cool would that be?

00:00:32.564 --> 00:00:33.966
With that said, you know,

00:00:33.966 --> 00:00:36.202
I haven't totally hated
the "me" time.

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:38.271
It's definitely allowed me
to get in touch with myself

00:00:38.271 --> 00:00:39.672
in a healthy way, and, you know,
if a guest was here

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:42.007
they'd probably want to
go on and on about

00:00:42.007 --> 00:00:44.076
whatever project they had,
and, you know,

00:00:44.076 --> 00:00:46.145
I don't -- I don't need that.

00:00:46.145 --> 00:00:49.882
Still, I don't think that would
be the case with Ethan Hawke.

00:00:49.882 --> 00:00:52.718
I mean, the Ethan Hawke.

00:00:52.718 --> 00:00:55.488
Does go on a bit.
Does go on a bit.

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:58.857
But he's Ethan Hawke! He's one
of my all-time favorite actors.

00:00:58.857 --> 00:01:01.260
Love me some Ethan Hawke.

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:03.262
Of course, knowing Ethan,
he'd probably have some sort

00:01:03.262 --> 00:01:06.065
of psychopath man-in-the-woods
beard right now

00:01:06.065 --> 00:01:08.668
and wouldn't be
that camera-ready.

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:10.736
Yeah, all things --
all things considered,

00:01:10.736 --> 00:01:13.172
it's good not having Ethan Hawke
right now.

00:01:13.172 --> 00:01:16.542
Anyway, I know it was
a long time ago,

00:01:16.542 --> 00:01:17.910
and I probably shouldn't
even say this.

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:19.979
I thought in "Dead Poets"
when he stood on the desk

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:21.581
and said, "O Captain!
My Captain!"

00:01:21.581 --> 00:01:24.183
it was just a little,
I don't know, showoff-y?

00:01:24.183 --> 00:01:28.554
-It was a character!

00:01:28.554 --> 00:01:30.556
-Anyway,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:01:30.556 --> 00:01:34.193 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:34.193 --> 00:01:36.562
In this moment, protesters
across the country

00:01:36.562 --> 00:01:38.797
are demanding an end
to institutional racism

00:01:38.797 --> 00:01:40.266
and police brutality,

00:01:40.266 --> 00:01:42.835
the coronavirus pandemic is
spiking in more than 20 states,

00:01:42.835 --> 00:01:44.570
our election infrastructure
is falling apart,

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:46.873
and millions of Americans
are camping out for hours

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:49.442
just to file for unemployment
amid a historic economic crisis.

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:51.677
I mean, look at this.
This is insane.

00:01:51.677 --> 00:01:53.779
Normally, you only see people
camped out on the sidewalk

00:01:53.779 --> 00:01:55.448
like this when there's
a new iPhone

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:57.016
or Harry Styles is hosting
"SNL,"

00:01:57.016 --> 00:01:59.418
an episode, by the way,
that I couldn't get tickets to,

00:01:59.418 --> 00:02:01.787
which is crazy because I had
a bit of a run there.

00:02:01.787 --> 00:02:03.623
This is truly, truly barbaric.

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:04.958
If you're a billion-dollar
corporation,

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:06.225
you can just call up
the government,

00:02:06.225 --> 00:02:07.793
you get a loan
you don't even need.

00:02:07.793 --> 00:02:09.762
But if you lose your job
thanks to a pandemic

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:11.263
the government failed to stop,

00:02:11.263 --> 00:02:13.532
you have to line up in the heat
for hours like you're waiting

00:02:13.532 --> 00:02:14.734
for a porta-potty at Ozzfest.

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:16.669
And as Ozzy himself would say,
our country is

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:20.539
♪ Going off the rails
on a crazy train ♪

00:02:20.539 --> 00:02:21.807
Yes.

00:02:21.807 --> 00:02:23.409
Anyway, I just hope
it's not too late

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:25.744
to learn how to love
and forget how to hate.

00:02:25.744 --> 00:02:29.515
That was for older brothers
born between, what, '63 and '71?

00:02:29.515 --> 00:02:32.484
The point is we're in a moment
of acute national crisis,

00:02:32.484 --> 00:02:34.787
thanks in large part
to the maligned negligence

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:37.724
of this taxidermied
business husk.

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:41.093
Wow! How'd the sales trip go,
Willy Loman?

00:02:41.093 --> 00:02:44.196
I hope Biff didn't wander in
on you and a strange woman.

00:02:44.196 --> 00:02:47.266
That would send him
in a long tailspin.

00:02:47.266 --> 00:02:48.734
What happened to you?

00:02:48.734 --> 00:02:50.403
You look like you just coached
the Knicks to a 50-point loss.

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:52.571
You should be standing
next to Jack Lemmon

00:02:52.571 --> 00:02:54.974
begging for
the Glenn Gary leads.

00:02:54.974 --> 00:02:56.342
We should never
have to see the president

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:58.744
in such a pathetic state.
It's embarrassing.

00:02:58.744 --> 00:03:01.680
The president is supposed to
project confidence and strength.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:04.183
Trump, on the other hand,
looks like a drunk wedding guest

00:03:04.183 --> 00:03:05.551
shuffling back to the Marriott.

00:03:05.551 --> 00:03:07.854
[ As Trump ] Or was it a Hyatt.

00:03:07.854 --> 00:03:09.155
[ Normal voice ] This is
like when you stay up

00:03:09.155 --> 00:03:11.223
past your bedtime and catch
a glimpse of your dad

00:03:11.223 --> 00:03:13.126
coming home late from work
totally plastered.

00:03:13.126 --> 00:03:15.294
Somehow,
this is the perfect imagine

00:03:15.294 --> 00:03:16.763
to sum up the Trump presidency.

00:03:16.763 --> 00:03:19.132
Now we just have to change
the presidential seal

00:03:19.132 --> 00:03:21.133
to a drunk eagle snoozing
in a BarcaLounger

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:23.603
with a beer in one hand
and remote control in the other.

00:03:23.603 --> 00:03:27.540
And I know. I know eagle's hands
are called claws.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.875
I made a mistake.
But it's tempting --

00:03:29.875 --> 00:03:32.011
Or maybe they're called talons.

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:33.279
Well, I should have
looked this up.

00:03:33.279 --> 00:03:34.948
But as tempting as it may be
to think that Trump

00:03:34.948 --> 00:03:36.282
somehow created all the problems

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:37.817
our country is facing,
he did not.

00:03:37.817 --> 00:03:39.051
He certainly made them worse,

00:03:39.051 --> 00:03:40.753
and in many cases,
profited from them.

00:03:40.753 --> 00:03:44.056
But the structural inequities
and institutional failures

00:03:44.056 --> 00:03:45.925
we're seeing right now
long predated him.

00:03:45.925 --> 00:03:48.227
They were created in part
by guys like Johnny Bolton

00:03:48.227 --> 00:03:50.262
over here, the ex-National
Security Advisor

00:03:50.262 --> 00:03:52.764
who refused to testify
at Trump's impeachment

00:03:52.764 --> 00:03:56.135
and is now hawking a book
called "Mustache Rides Again."

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:58.737
Oh, wait, I think it's called
"The Trash Behind the Stache."

00:03:58.737 --> 00:04:00.706
No, wait, you know what, guys?
I think it's called

00:04:00.706 --> 00:04:02.875
"Boltin' Bolton's Butt Ton
of Bull Dung."

00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:04.677
Anyway, you can find it
on Amazon

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:07.446
under the "Please Light Your
Money on Fire Instead" section.

00:04:07.446 --> 00:04:09.882
John Bolton is an unrepentant
warmonger who has helped

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:11.984
usher in some
of the worst calamities

00:04:11.984 --> 00:04:15.421
of the last two decades and who
epitomizes our era of venal,

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:17.623
self-serving sociopaths
burning everything down

00:04:17.623 --> 00:04:19.225
and then cashing in
as they slink away.

00:04:19.225 --> 00:04:21.060
But other than that,
he a great guy.

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:23.896
Last night, Bolton was on ABC
trying to sell his book

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:25.531
about his time
in the Trump White House.

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:26.833
Trump, a man, let's not forget,

00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:29.902
he voted for and then lobbied
to get a job with.

00:04:29.902 --> 00:04:31.671
-I don't think he's fit
for office.

00:04:31.671 --> 00:04:34.306
I don't think he has the
competence to carry out the job.

00:04:34.306 --> 00:04:37.510
-You supported Donald Trump
during the 2016 election.

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:40.446
You watched his first 15 months
in office.

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:43.715
What did you think of the job
he was doing up to that point?

00:04:43.715 --> 00:04:46.886
-I think I made a mistake.
-No, I don't think he did.

00:04:46.886 --> 00:04:48.087
I don't think he made a mistake.

00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:50.155
I think you're a remora,

00:04:50.155 --> 00:04:53.026
you know those little fish
that swim alongside sharks

00:04:53.026 --> 00:04:54.227
and eat whatever they miss?

00:04:54.227 --> 00:04:56.062
That's what all these
Trump White House

00:04:56.062 --> 00:04:57.296
supporting cast members are.

00:04:57.296 --> 00:04:58.698
And then,
when their bellies are full,

00:04:58.698 --> 00:05:01.067
they swim out of the White House
and write a book called,

00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:03.703
"Damn, That Shark Was Crazy!"

00:05:03.703 --> 00:05:06.772
"I think a made a mistake"
is not how you talk about

00:05:06.772 --> 00:05:09.074
enthusiastically supporting
and working for

00:05:09.074 --> 00:05:11.410
a racist authoritarian
who's trampling our democracy

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:12.478
for his own self-interest.

00:05:12.478 --> 00:05:14.146
That's what you say when you get

00:05:14.146 --> 00:05:15.815
the Domino's order and realize

00:05:15.815 --> 00:05:17.517
it has peppers
instead of pepperoni.

00:05:17.517 --> 00:05:20.152
"Oh, damn it.
I think I made a mistake.

00:05:20.152 --> 00:05:24.390
I meant to get pizza, but
instead I ordered Domino's."

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:26.125
Bolton didn't make a mistake.

00:05:26.125 --> 00:05:27.993
He saw Trump in 2016

00:05:27.993 --> 00:05:29.962
and throughout the first half
of his presidency

00:05:29.962 --> 00:05:31.764
promising to rip up
the Iran deal

00:05:31.764 --> 00:05:33.799
and to kill the families
of terrorists

00:05:33.799 --> 00:05:35.200
and banning of Muslims,

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:37.303
and he thought he could use
Trump to get what he wanted.

00:05:37.303 --> 00:05:39.071
It only backfired
when he realized Trump's like

00:05:39.071 --> 00:05:40.539
a tiger in a circus act.

00:05:40.539 --> 00:05:42.842
He starts out friendly,
but one wrong move,

00:05:42.842 --> 00:05:45.044
and he will lunge for your face.

00:05:45.044 --> 00:05:46.679
People like Bolton are
a big part of the reason

00:05:46.679 --> 00:05:48.547
we're in this mess in the first
place, and on top of that,

00:05:48.547 --> 00:05:51.317
the structural inequities
in our sham democracy

00:05:51.317 --> 00:05:53.519
ensure that a party with
a disastrous 20-year record

00:05:53.519 --> 00:05:55.554
of governance over the course
of two historically

00:05:55.554 --> 00:05:57.756
awful presidents
can keep winning elections.

00:05:57.756 --> 00:06:01.126
They don't need to be popular
if voter suppression

00:06:01.126 --> 00:06:03.662
and an antiquated
electoral college system

00:06:03.662 --> 00:06:04.930
can keep them in power.

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:06.599
And sure enough, the Trump team

00:06:06.599 --> 00:06:09.435
is already sending signals
that they plan to interfere

00:06:09.435 --> 00:06:12.104
with the actual administration
of the election.

00:06:12.104 --> 00:06:14.674
This weekend, for example,
the Attorney General Bill Barr

00:06:14.674 --> 00:06:17.509
repeated a series of obvious
lies about mail-in voting,

00:06:17.509 --> 00:06:20.112
which many state officials,
including Republicans,

00:06:20.112 --> 00:06:22.614
have turned to as a safe
alternative during the pandemic.

00:06:22.614 --> 00:06:25.584
Barr claimed falsely
that mail-in ballots

00:06:25.584 --> 00:06:27.787
somehow open the floodgates
to fraud.

00:06:27.787 --> 00:06:30.423
-Well, there's a big discussion
right now about mail-in voting.

00:06:30.423 --> 00:06:33.158
Hillary Clinton said it's fine,
it's fair.

00:06:33.158 --> 00:06:37.163
-Well, it absolutely opens
the floodgates to fraud.

00:06:37.163 --> 00:06:39.197
Those things
are delivered into mailboxes.

00:06:39.197 --> 00:06:40.566
They can be taken out.

00:06:40.566 --> 00:06:43.335
There's questions about
whether or not it even denies

00:06:43.335 --> 00:06:46.706
a secret ballot because a lot
of the states have you signing

00:06:46.706 --> 00:06:48.341
the outside of the envelope,

00:06:48.341 --> 00:06:50.977
so the person
who opens the envelope

00:06:50.977 --> 00:06:52.979
will know how people voted.

00:06:52.979 --> 00:06:56.883
There's no -- Right now,
a foreign country could print up

00:06:56.883 --> 00:07:00.653
tens of thousands
of counterfeit ballots

00:07:00.653 --> 00:07:03.155
and it'd be very hard for us
to detect which was the right

00:07:03.155 --> 00:07:06.125
and which was the wrong ballot.
So I think it can --

00:07:06.125 --> 00:07:09.462
it can upset and undercut
the confidence

00:07:09.462 --> 00:07:11.764
in the integrity
of our elections.

00:07:11.764 --> 00:07:13.132
-You know what upsets confidence

00:07:13.132 --> 00:07:14.567
in the integrity
of our elections?

00:07:14.567 --> 00:07:16.302
People having to stand in line
to vote like they're waiting

00:07:16.302 --> 00:07:18.437
to take pictures with the mall
Santa on December 23rd.

00:07:18.437 --> 00:07:20.206
Of course,
if Bill Barr was in charge,

00:07:20.206 --> 00:07:21.740
they'd have to line up
on August 8th.

00:07:21.740 --> 00:07:23.342
Second,
none of what you said is true.

00:07:23.342 --> 00:07:26.211
You can't just print up fake
mail ballots and send them in.

00:07:26.211 --> 00:07:28.214
You know they still check
to make sure

00:07:28.214 --> 00:07:29.515
they're from registered voters,
right?

00:07:29.515 --> 00:07:31.617
It's not like you could just
write on a piece of paper

00:07:31.617 --> 00:07:34.420
"I vote for Joe Exotic" and send
it to the Board of Elections,

00:07:34.420 --> 00:07:37.189
although honestly, at this rate,
I'm desperate enough to try it.

00:07:37.189 --> 00:07:39.625
Hey!
I think he's learned his lesson.

00:07:39.625 --> 00:07:41.827
I saw some real growth from Joe.

00:07:41.827 --> 00:07:44.597
And then this morning,
Trump himself tweeted...

00:07:49.668 --> 00:07:51.336
They're trying to cheat
by disrupting

00:07:51.336 --> 00:07:53.205
the actual administration
of the election,

00:07:53.205 --> 00:07:55.407
and that's because they're
so worried that if voters

00:07:55.407 --> 00:07:57.042
get to vote fairly,
he won't win.

00:07:57.042 --> 00:07:58.543
Donald Trump is now
and has always been

00:07:58.543 --> 00:08:00.178
a historically unpopular
president.

00:08:00.178 --> 00:08:02.114
He's just been able to mask
his unpopularity

00:08:02.114 --> 00:08:03.850
and soothe his ego
with large crowds

00:08:03.850 --> 00:08:06.719
at his mosh pit/group therapy
sessions,

00:08:06.719 --> 00:08:08.955
which is why his rally
in Tulsa on Saturday,

00:08:08.955 --> 00:08:11.357
his first in months,
was planned as a big show

00:08:11.357 --> 00:08:13.358
of political strength, nevermind
the fact that Tulsa

00:08:13.358 --> 00:08:15.895
is a coronavirus hotspot
with spiking numbers

00:08:15.895 --> 00:08:17.429
that have alarmed
local health officials.

00:08:17.429 --> 00:08:20.565
Trump disregarded that just
to make himself feel better.

00:08:20.565 --> 00:08:22.535
Beforehand, Trump base told CNN

00:08:22.535 --> 00:08:24.237
that the rally wasn't
just about politics.

00:08:24.237 --> 00:08:26.372
It was...

00:08:38.216 --> 00:08:39.985
You know what else
is good for that? Prozac.

00:08:39.985 --> 00:08:42.121
You just slip some
into his hamburger,

00:08:42.121 --> 00:08:43.856
you know, the way you
give pills to a dog.

00:08:43.856 --> 00:08:46.993
Or slap a label on the bottle
that says, "Hydroxychloroquine."

00:08:46.993 --> 00:08:49.028
[ As Trump ]
This stuff cures neverything.

00:08:49.028 --> 00:08:50.496
[ Normal voice ]
Think about that --

00:08:50.496 --> 00:08:53.599
The president held an indoor
rally at a coronavirus hotspot,

00:08:53.599 --> 00:08:55.100
putting people's lives at risk

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:56.768
just to make himself
feel better.

00:08:56.768 --> 00:08:59.371
Can't we just get that truck
back to the White House lawn

00:08:59.371 --> 00:09:01.073
and let him honk the horn
a few times?

00:09:01.073 --> 00:09:02.475
"Do you feel better,
Mr. President?"

00:09:02.475 --> 00:09:05.844
[ As Trump ] I am feeling
a little bit better.

00:09:05.844 --> 00:09:07.913
[ Normal voice ] At this rate,
he should be doing his rallies

00:09:07.913 --> 00:09:10.516
on a fainting couch
while a doctor takes notes.

00:09:10.516 --> 00:09:12.551
Still, there you go --
The president's aides

00:09:12.551 --> 00:09:15.487
said Saturday's rally would
put him in a much better mood,

00:09:15.487 --> 00:09:17.323
and clearly,
Trump was looking forward to it

00:09:17.323 --> 00:09:19.125
because he spent all week
bragging

00:09:19.125 --> 00:09:21.527
about the number of people
who had RSVP'd.

00:09:21.527 --> 00:09:26.532
-They have a new, a pretty new,
magnificent arena,

00:09:26.532 --> 00:09:28.868
as you probably have heard.

00:09:28.868 --> 00:09:31.269
And we're getting
exact numbers out,

00:09:31.269 --> 00:09:34.673
but we're either close
to or over one million people

00:09:34.673 --> 00:09:36.309
wanting to go.

00:09:36.309 --> 00:09:38.510
We have a 22,000-seat arena,

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:41.446
but I think we're gonna
also take the convention hall

00:09:41.446 --> 00:09:43.715
next door,
and that's gonna hold 40,000.

00:09:43.715 --> 00:09:45.717
So we'll have 22,000,
plus 40,000,

00:09:45.717 --> 00:09:48.687
which would mean that we'd
have over 900,000 people

00:09:48.687 --> 00:09:52.424
that won't be able to go, but
hopefully they'll be watching.

00:09:52.424 --> 00:09:56.329
But it's an amazing -- Nobody's
ever heard of numbers like this.

00:09:56.329 --> 00:09:58.998
-You got to love how Trump
thinks a success is a situation

00:09:58.998 --> 00:10:01.166
in which 90% of his supporters
get screwed.

00:10:01.166 --> 00:10:02.935
[ As Trump ] Also,
we have a baked potato bar,

00:10:02.935 --> 00:10:05.370
all the fixings for everyone
who doesn't get in.

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:07.840
Just the two potatoes, though,
so show up early.

00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:10.242
[ Normal voice ] Nobody's ever
heard numbers like this?

00:10:10.242 --> 00:10:12.077
You know what number of people
have heard?

00:10:12.077 --> 00:10:14.747
6,200, the actual number
of people who showed up,

00:10:14.747 --> 00:10:16.949
according to the fire marshall,
and that fire marshall

00:10:16.949 --> 00:10:18.984
was probably the only person in
Tulsa who had a good night.

00:10:18.984 --> 00:10:21.120
He was like, "Oh, this is great.
If there's a fire,

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:23.022
we'll get everybody out of here
in, like, 30 seconds."

00:10:23.022 --> 00:10:25.357
Trump's team kept ramping up
expectations.

00:10:25.357 --> 00:10:28.360
His campaign manager
Brad Parscale bragged

00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:30.896
that a million people --
a million people had RSVP'd

00:10:30.896 --> 00:10:32.931
and that they'd have a total
of close to 100,000.

00:10:32.931 --> 00:10:35.300
You guys sure you want to
call your shot like that?

00:10:35.300 --> 00:10:36.435
You're like a basketball player

00:10:36.435 --> 00:10:38.537
giving
a pre-game press conference

00:10:38.537 --> 00:10:39.771
about how many points he scored.

00:10:39.771 --> 00:10:40.939
"You know, I just want
to thank God

00:10:40.939 --> 00:10:42.408
and my teammates
for supporting me.

00:10:42.408 --> 00:10:45.010
It wasn't easy to score a 50
in a game, but I did it.

00:10:45.010 --> 00:10:47.479
All right. I'm gonna go warm up.
Achilles is pretty tight."

00:10:47.479 --> 00:10:50.148
Although my favorite,
favorite Trump prediction

00:10:50.148 --> 00:10:51.183
has to be this one.

00:10:51.183 --> 00:10:53.118
-And we expect to have --
you know,

00:10:53.118 --> 00:10:54.386
it's like
a record-setting crowd.

00:10:54.386 --> 00:10:56.221
We've never had an empty seat.

00:10:56.221 --> 00:10:58.089
And we certainly won't
in Oklahoma.

00:10:58.089 --> 00:11:00.959
-We certainly won't have
an empty seat in Oklahoma.

00:11:00.959 --> 00:11:02.261
It's too perfect.

00:11:02.261 --> 00:11:04.663
This is like if Babe Ruth
had pointed to center field

00:11:04.663 --> 00:11:06.999
and then stepped into the box
and fouled one off his ankle.

00:11:06.999 --> 00:11:08.700
"Oh [bleep]!

00:11:08.700 --> 00:11:12.671
Oh, no, I think I broke it!
Oh [bleep]!

00:11:12.671 --> 00:11:15.440
Can you edit out the part
where I pointed?

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:18.610
We're live?! Oh [bleep]!"

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:22.147
So the president banked
not only his political comeback

00:11:22.147 --> 00:11:24.783
but his mood in a big show
of force in Tulsa.

00:11:24.783 --> 00:11:27.086
And then, you know,
this happened.

00:11:27.086 --> 00:11:29.021
-President Trump's
first campaign rally

00:11:29.021 --> 00:11:31.790
in more than 100 days
drew controversy

00:11:31.790 --> 00:11:34.026
and a smaller-than-expected
crowd.

00:11:34.026 --> 00:11:36.995
The upper decks of the arena
there in Tulsa, Oklahoma,

00:11:36.995 --> 00:11:38.096
were largely empty.

00:11:38.096 --> 00:11:40.032
-There were plenty of empty
seats

00:11:40.032 --> 00:11:42.801
in the 19,000-capacity BOK
Center.

00:11:42.801 --> 00:11:45.738
-But in the end, the president
was a bit of a bust in Tulsa.

00:11:45.738 --> 00:11:47.640
Campaign quickly dismantling
one venue.

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:49.975
That other venue,
about one-third full.

00:11:49.975 --> 00:11:53.112
Tulsa's fire department
saying about 6,200 people

00:11:53.112 --> 00:11:56.848
showed up in an arena that held
19,000 for the president.

00:11:56.848 --> 00:11:59.551
Wow, I've seen less empty seats
at an improv show.

00:11:59.551 --> 00:12:01.420
And, let's be honest,
Trump's rallies are basically

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:03.522
an improv show where he gives
himself his own suggestion.

00:12:03.522 --> 00:12:05.291
[ As Trump ] Can I have the name
of a famous person?

00:12:05.291 --> 00:12:06.658
I heard Hillary.

00:12:06.658 --> 00:12:08.493
[ Normal voice ] The arena
wasn't even one-third full.

00:12:08.493 --> 00:12:10.295
Trump staked his political
fortunes and his ego

00:12:10.295 --> 00:12:11.864
on this rally, and it was such
a flop,

00:12:11.864 --> 00:12:14.232
they even had to cancel
a planned second speech

00:12:14.232 --> 00:12:16.635
to what they thought would be
an overflow crowd outside.

00:12:16.635 --> 00:12:18.570
Before Trump had landed,
crews were literally

00:12:18.570 --> 00:12:21.840
breaking down the stage because
so few people were there.

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:23.876
Wow! He's the President
of the United States,

00:12:23.876 --> 00:12:25.644
and they're treating him
like the least popular band

00:12:25.644 --> 00:12:26.978
at Coachella.

00:12:26.978 --> 00:12:29.147
"Sorry, bro, I guess everybody
went over to see Beyoncé.

00:12:29.147 --> 00:12:31.983
You can keep the lanyards
if you want.

00:12:31.983 --> 00:12:34.319
What kind of music do you guys
do anyway? Rage rap?"

00:12:34.319 --> 00:12:37.556
And Trump's performance was just
as lackluster as the attendance.

00:12:37.556 --> 00:12:39.859
You'd think at a moment like
this, the president might

00:12:39.859 --> 00:12:42.294
want to offer soothing words
about the state of the nation

00:12:42.294 --> 00:12:43.828
and the various crises we face.

00:12:43.828 --> 00:12:48.000
Instead, Trump spent one
of every eight minutes in Tulsa

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:50.468
complaining about coverage
of his West Point speech.

00:12:50.468 --> 00:12:52.471
Specifically, he complained
about the coverage

00:12:52.471 --> 00:12:54.006
of the way he tiptoed
down a ramp

00:12:54.006 --> 00:12:56.474
like a toddler on ice skates,
and the way he drank water.

00:12:56.474 --> 00:12:59.344
-So then my wife said,

00:12:59.344 --> 00:13:03.081
"Well, it wasn't only the ramp.

00:13:03.081 --> 00:13:05.083
Did you have water?"

00:13:05.083 --> 00:13:07.887
So what happens is I said, "What
does it have to do with water?"

00:13:07.887 --> 00:13:10.989
They said,
"You couldn't lift your hand up

00:13:10.989 --> 00:13:12.624
to your mouth with water."

00:13:12.624 --> 00:13:15.060
She said,
"Well, I know what you did.

00:13:15.060 --> 00:13:17.496
You had on a very good red tie."

00:13:17.496 --> 00:13:20.933
And I don't want to get water
on the tie.

00:13:20.933 --> 00:13:24.836
And I don't want to drink much.
So I lifted up the water.

00:13:24.836 --> 00:13:26.471
I see we have a little glass
of water.

00:13:26.471 --> 00:13:27.973
Where the hell did this water
come from?

00:13:27.973 --> 00:13:29.941
[ Cheers and applause ]
So I put it up to my lip,

00:13:29.941 --> 00:13:35.046
and then I say, because
I don't want it -- Just in case.

00:13:35.046 --> 00:13:37.116
And they gave me
another disease.

00:13:37.116 --> 00:13:41.220
[ Laughter ]
They gave me another disease.

00:13:41.220 --> 00:13:43.822
[ Laughter ]

00:13:43.822 --> 00:13:45.958
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:13:53.532 --> 00:13:57.769
-Seriously, has a president's
base ever set a lower bar?

00:13:57.769 --> 00:14:02.274
"Whoo! That arm works!
That arm works!"

00:14:02.274 --> 00:14:05.043
The crowd cheered the president
drinking water with one hand

00:14:05.043 --> 00:14:07.145
the way NASA cheered when
they landed a rover on Mars.

00:14:07.145 --> 00:14:08.847
That's not supposed
to be impressive.

00:14:08.847 --> 00:14:10.882
"Good news, he's drinking water
with one hand" is something

00:14:10.882 --> 00:14:13.051
a doctor would say to you about
a loved one who was recently

00:14:13.051 --> 00:14:14.653
hit on the head by a falling can
of paint.

00:14:14.653 --> 00:14:16.255
"He's regained motor function
in his right arm.

00:14:16.255 --> 00:14:18.424
Unfortunately, he is, um...

00:14:18.424 --> 00:14:19.824
he is still having trouble
with the ramp."

00:14:19.824 --> 00:14:22.160
Although the biggest lie
in that story might be the idea

00:14:22.160 --> 00:14:23.828
that he had a conversation
with his wife.

00:14:23.828 --> 00:14:25.731
And even if he did, what
a horrible conversation.

00:14:25.731 --> 00:14:28.334
Her first question to you
was, "Did you have water?"

00:14:28.334 --> 00:14:31.369
That's not a question you ask
a president or a loved one.

00:14:31.369 --> 00:14:33.739
That's a question you ask
a sick cat.

00:14:33.739 --> 00:14:35.707
The president staked
his political fortunes

00:14:35.707 --> 00:14:37.208
on a rally
that turned out to be a dud

00:14:37.208 --> 00:14:39.912
amid a series of mounting crises
that have deflated

00:14:39.912 --> 00:14:42.247
his already historically bad
poll numbers.

00:14:42.247 --> 00:14:44.983
It's a reminder that this
president is deeply unpopular.

00:14:44.983 --> 00:14:48.053
And his only hope of getting
re-elected is by scaring people

00:14:48.053 --> 00:14:50.188
and undermining the integrity
of the election itself.

00:14:50.188 --> 00:14:52.791
And when he and his campaign
look back on their decision

00:14:52.791 --> 00:14:55.060
to brag so much about this rally
in advance,

00:14:55.060 --> 00:14:56.828
I bet they'll say
to themselves...

00:14:56.828 --> 00:14:58.697
-I think I made a mistake.

00:14:58.697 --> 00:15:00.565
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:15:00.565 --> 00:15:03.969 line:0%
♪♪

00:15:03.969 --> 00:15:06.471 line:0%
As New York works hard to reopen
under phase two,

00:15:06.471 --> 00:15:08.473 line:0%
remember that we're still a city
in crisis.

00:15:08.473 --> 00:15:10.042 line:0%
And City Harvest
has been stepping up

00:15:10.042 --> 00:15:11.510 line:0%
to meet the increased need.

00:15:11.510 --> 00:15:13.845 line:0%
If you're watching this online,
you can hit the "donate" button.

00:15:13.845 --> 00:15:16.882 line:0%
Stay safe, wash your hands,
we love you.

